<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<xmile version="1.0" level="3" xmlns="http://www.systemdynamics.org/XMILE" xmlns:isee="http://iseesystems.com/XMILE">
    <header>
        <smile version="1.0" namespace="std, isee">
            <uses_arrays>1</uses_arrays>
        </smile>
        <name>Lesson4MODELING</name>
        <uuid>63d212a4-b1d9-46e3-b698-9ebd75f717e7</uuid>
        <vendor>isee systems, inc.</vendor>
        <product version="10.1.2" isee:saved_by_v1="false" lang="en">iThink</product>
    </header>
    <style>
        <model font-family="Arial" font-size="12" />
        <interface font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
    </style>
    <sim_specs method="Euler" time_units="Weeks" pause_interval="2" isee:pause_after_rates="false" isee:instantaneous_flows="false">
        <start>0</start>
        <stop>10</stop>
        <dt>1</dt>
    </sim_specs>
    <dimensions>
        <dim name="Dim_Name_1" size="1" />
    </dimensions>
    <model_units />
    <isee:prefs last_model="true" layer="model" grid_width="20" grid_height="50" divide_by_zero_alert="true" hide_taskbar="true" show_module_prefix="true">
        <isee:window width="858" height="610" />
        <isee:security />
        <isee:print_setup width="818" height="572" />
    </isee:prefs>
    <isee:equation_prefs order_by="module" />
    <model>
        <stock name="TOTAL_FOOD\nIN_FOOD_BANK">
            <doc>The STOCK of TOTAL FOOD IN FOOD BANK is defined by the initial supply of food on shelves. &#x0D;&#x0D;In the simulation, the initial Stock of TOTAL FOOD IN FOOD BANK was 600 pounds.&#x0D;&#x0D;To change this number, type in a new amount and click OK.</doc>
            <eqn>600</eqn>
            <scale min="0" max="1200" />
            <inflow>Weekly_Food_Donations</inflow>
            <outflow>Food_Distributed_Weekly</outflow>
            <non_negative />
            <event_poster min="0.1" max="160">
                <threshold value="1" direction="decreasing">
                    <event sim_action="stop">
                        <text_box>The Food Bank no longer has any more food on its shelves. What happened?  Information in the Table may help you understand what happened.&#x0D;What could you have done to have prevented this?&#x0D;Would you care to try again?</text_box>
                    </event>
                </threshold>
            </event_poster>
            <display x="389" y="748" color="red" label_angle="80">
                <scale min="0" max="1200" />
            </display>
        </stock>
        <flow name="Weekly_Food\nDonations">
            <doc>This equation records 10 weekly food donations that add pounds of food to the Food Bank shelves.&#x0D;&#x0D;To change this equation, click &quot;Hide Document,&quot; then make changes and click OK. </doc>
            <eqn>If time &gt; 9 then 0 else food_donations_each_week</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="302" y="748" color="black" label_side="top" label_angle="104">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="237" y="748" />
                    <pt x="367" y="748" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="Week_#">
            <doc>This is used to record the week # of the simulation. </doc>
            <eqn>min(time + 1, 10)</eqn>
            <display x="263" y="928" color="blue" />
        </aux>
        <flow name="Food\nDistributed_Weekly">
            <doc>The number of pounds of food distributed weekly is equal to the amount of food (in pounds distributed) per family) multiplied by the number of families assisted.&#x0D;&#x0D;To change this equation, click on the &quot;Hide Document&quot; button, make the desired changes, and click OK.</doc>
            <eqn>food_per__family*number_of_families_assisted</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="476" y="748" color="red" label_side="top" label_angle="35">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="411" y="748" />
                    <pt x="541" y="748" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="food_per_\nfamily">
            <doc>In the simulation, families receive 30 pounds of food per week. &#x0D;&#x0D;Type in a new number to change food per family and click OK.</doc>
            <eqn>30</eqn>
            <display x="441" y="818" color="fuchsia" />
        </aux>
        <stock name="TOTAL_FOOD\nDISTRIBUTED">
            <doc>This is the TOTAL (number of pounds of) FOOD DISTRIBUTED during the entire simulation.</doc>
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <inflow>Food__Distributed_Each_Week</inflow>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="379" y="931" color="red" />
        </stock>
        <flow name="Food_\nDistributed\nEach_Week">
            <doc>This flow of Food Distributed Weekly is used to calculate the TOTAL FOOD DISTRIBUTED during the simulation.</doc>
            <eqn>Food_Distributed_Weekly</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="437" y="930" color="red" label_angle="284">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="474" y="930" />
                    <pt x="401" y="930" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <aux name="food_donations\neach_week">
            <doc>In our simulation, we said that food donations had fallen recently from 350 to 300 pounds per week. &#x0D;&#x0D;Type in a new number to change food donations each week and click OK. </doc>
            <eqn>300</eqn>
            <display x="306" y="818" color="fuchsia" />
        </aux>
        <stock name="TOTAL_FOOD\nDONATIONS">
            <doc>This is the TOTAL (number of pounds of) FOOD DONATIONS during the entire simulation.</doc>
            <eqn>0</eqn>
            <inflow>Weekly_Donations</inflow>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="76" y="933" color="black" />
        </stock>
        <aux name="number_of\nfamilies_assisted">
            <doc>In the simulation, the number of families receiving weekly food donations was set at 15.&#x0D;&#x0D;Type in a new number to change number of families assisted and click OK.</doc>
            <eqn>15</eqn>
            <display x="517" y="820" color="fuchsia" label_angle="308" />
        </aux>
        <flow name="Weekly\nDonations">
            <doc>This flow is the number of pounds of Weekly Food Donations, and is used to calculate the  TOTAL FOOD DONATIONS during the entire simulation. </doc>
            <eqn>Weekly_Food_Donations</eqn>
            <non_negative />
            <display x="129" y="931" color="black" label_angle="309">
                <pts>
                    <pt x="161" y="931" />
                    <pt x="98" y="931" />
                </pts>
            </display>
        </flow>
        <display page_width="818" page_height="572" page_cols="2" page_rows="2" isee:converter_size="medium" isee:name_only_modules="true" isee:animate_flows="true" isee:animate_stocks="true">
            <connector x="188" y="982" uid="1" color="black">
                <from>
                    <alias uid="0" />
                </from>
                <to>Weekly_Donations</to>
            </connector>
            <alias x="191" y="990" uid="0">
                <of>Weekly_Food_Donations</of>
            </alias>
            <alias x="447" y="1004" uid="2">
                <of>Food_Distributed_Weekly</of>
                <label_angle>249</label_angle>
            </alias>
            <connector x="456" y="1001" uid="3">
                <from>
                    <alias uid="2" />
                </from>
                <to>Food__Distributed_Each_Week</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="439" y="809" uid="4" color="red">
                <from>food_per__family</from>
                <to>Food_Distributed_Weekly</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="312" y="812" uid="5" color="black">
                <from>food_donations_each_week</from>
                <to>Weekly_Food_Donations</to>
            </connector>
            <connector x="519" y="811" uid="6" color="red">
                <from>number_of_families_assisted</from>
                <to>Food_Distributed_Weekly</to>
            </connector>
            <stacked_container height="260" width="454" uid="7">
                <graph type="time_series" title="Untitled" background="#FFFE91" show_grid="true" plot_numbers="true" isee:use_five_segments="true" hide_detail="true" comparative="true" cleared="true" time_precision="2" from="0" to="10">
                    <plot index="0" pen_width="3" color="blue" precision="1" show_y_axis="true">
                        <scale auto="true" />
                        <entity name="TOTAL_FOOD_IN_FOOD_BANK" />
                    </plot>
                </graph>
            </stacked_container>
            <pad_icon x="683" y="820" width="26" height="22" color="#008F44" label_side="bottom" label="Graph 1" type="graph" icon_of="7" />
            <stacked_container height="269" width="527" uid="8">
                <table font-size="9" background="#E0E0E0" column_width="130" orientation="vertical" interval="1" cleared="true" date_time="2010-12-21T14:01:41Z">
                    <title>Untitled Table</title>
                    <item type="time" color="black" precision="max" width="47" />
                    <item color="black" precision="0.01" delimit_000s="true" index="0">
                        <entity name="Weekly_Food_Donations" />
                    </item>
                    <item color="black" precision="0.01" delimit_000s="true" index="1">
                        <entity name="TOTAL_FOOD_IN_FOOD_BANK" />
                    </item>
                    <item color="black" precision="0.01" delimit_000s="true" index="2">
                        <entity name="Food_Distributed_Weekly" />
                    </item>
                </table>
            </stacked_container>
            <pad_icon x="735" y="819" width="26" height="22" color="#008F44" label_side="bottom" label="Table 1" type="table" icon_of="8" />
            <numeric_display precision="1" delimit_000s="true" color="blue" show_name="true" retain_ending_value="true" uid="9" x="678" y="661">
                <entity name="Week_#" />
            </numeric_display>
            <numeric_display precision="0.01" display_as="number" color="red" show_name="true" retain_ending_value="true" uid="10" x="678" y="677">
                <entity name="TOTAL_FOOD_IN_FOOD_BANK" />
            </numeric_display>
            <button x="405" y="523" width="146" height="31" uid="11" appearance="opaque" background="red" color="white" style="square" label="Explore Model Used in Lesson 4" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="572" />
            </button>
            <text_box x="4" y="3" uid="12" color="red" font-family="Arial" font-size="32" font-weight="bold" text-align="center" padding="5" width="770" height="49">Can I Successfully Run the Local Food Bank?</text_box>
            <button x="277" y="47" width="183" height="30" uid="13" appearance="opaque" background="#0CA0FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="Intro: Build Your Own Model!" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <popup x="-184" y="40" width="617" height="346" background="yellow" color="black">
                    <text_box font-family="Arial" font-size="16">If you haven&apos;t modeled before, watch our Build Your Own Personal Finance Model video to help you get started with using STELLA modeling software, available at http://clexchange.org/curriculum/dollarsandsense.asp. &#x0D;&#x0D;Choose from 2 options:&#x0D;&#x0D;(1) Use this blank STELLA page to build your own model from scratch. Everything you need is here (icons/buttons for building blocks, tables and graphs, text; Word menus to run and print...);  OR&#x0D;&#x0D;(2) Click on the &quot;Explore Model Used in Lesson 4&quot; to explore a version of the actual model used in Lesson 4 (It&apos;s actually a very simple model and everything in it is explained!). &#x0D;&#x0D;Start wherever you want! Play with it and have fun!&#x0D;&#x0D;</text_box>
                </popup>
            </button>
            <button x="401" y="1107" width="146" height="31" uid="14" appearance="opaque" background="#E0E0E0" color="white" style="square" label="Explore Model Used in Lesson 4" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="572" />
            </button>
            <button x="1146" y="693" width="129" height="34" uid="15" appearance="opaque" background="#0CA0FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="What can I do with this?" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <popup x="-124" y="286" width="422" height="204" background="yellow" color="black">
                    <text_box font-family="Arial" font-size="16">This is a version of the model underlying the Lesson 3 Simulation. When you click and open any building block, you will find an explanation for how it works. &#x0D;&#x0D;You will notice that the factors effecting &quot;Daily Income&quot; (price per cup, Daily Cups Actually Sold) and &quot;Daily Expenses&quot; (batches made, cost per batch) have changed.  Why do you think we put that in? Click on these building blocks to learn more.&#x0D;&#x0D;Expore how you can make changes (e.g., change numbers; rename or add new building blocks to make this &quot;your&quot; model). Have fun!</text_box>
                </popup>
            </button>
            <button x="242" y="523" width="147" height="32" uid="16" appearance="opaque" background="#E0E0E0" color="white" style="square" label="Build Your Own Model " font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="0" />
            </button>
            <text_box x="24" y="568" uid="17" color="red" font-family="Comic Sans MS" font-size="32" font-weight="bold" text-align="center" padding="5" width="746" height="56"> Model Used in Lesson 4</text_box>
            <button x="598" y="925" width="65" height="34" uid="18" appearance="opaque" background="#7F00FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="Run" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <menu_action>run</menu_action>
            </button>
            <button x="674" y="925" width="65" height="34" uid="19" appearance="opaque" background="#7F00FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="Reset" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <menu_action>restore_all</menu_action>
            </button>
            <button x="346" y="628" width="129" height="34" uid="20" appearance="opaque" background="#0CA0FF" color="white" style="rounded" label="What can I do with this?" font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <popup x="-119" y="282" width="389" height="204" background="yellow" color="black">
                    <text_box font-family="Arial" font-size="16">Here&apos;s the actual Stock and Flow model used in Lesson 4. It is a relatively simple model.  &quot;Food donations each week &quot; affect the rate that pounds of food flow into the STOCK of TOTAL FOOD IN FOOD BANK. &quot;Food Distributed Weekly,&quot; based on &quot;number of families assisted&quot; and pounds of &quot;food per family&quot; affect the rate that Food flows out of the Food Bank.. &#x0D;&#x0D;Explore (e.g., change any of the amounts; rename or add new building blocks to make this your model). Play with it and have fun!&#x0D;</text_box>
                </popup>
            </button>
            <button x="244" y="1106" width="147" height="32" uid="21" appearance="opaque" background="red" color="white" style="square" label="Build Your Own Model " font-family="Arial" font-size="12" text-align="center">
                <link target="model" x="0" y="0" />
            </button>
            <style font-family="Arial" font-size="12" />
        </display>
        <interface show_pages="true" page_cols="3" page_rows="3" page_width="788" page_height="528" zoom="12.5">
            <simulation_delay>0.01</simulation_delay>
            <style font-family="Arial" font-size="9" />
        </interface>
        <popup x="45" y="224" content="7" />
        <popup x="274" y="187" content="8" />
        <style font-family="Arial" font-size="12" />
    </model>
</xmile>
